course: dictionary
lesson: 10629
title: Moments that stay with you
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Unforgettable is made of three parts: un- (not), forget (to lose from memory) and -able (can be). So something unforgettable is something you cannot easily forget. «We had an unforgettable day at the seaside.» The day was so good that you will remember it for a long time.
explain: The word is not only about good things. The dictionary says the moment can be special, exciting, beautiful or strange. «The trip was an unforgettable adventure.» Adventure is a clue: a trip full of new and exciting things is the kind of thing you remember.
explain: Look at the words around it. Words like day, trip, holiday, experience or event often sit next to it. Then ask yourself: would I still remember this in a year? If yes, the word is probably unforgettable.
fact: Unforgettable is an adjective: it describes a noun, like «an unforgettable day».
fact: Un- means not, forget means to lose from memory, and -able means can be.
fact: «Unforgettable» means so special, exciting, beautiful or strange that you will remember it for a very long time.
fact: «Iconic» means unforgettable, so it is a synonym: a word with a similar meaning.
fact: Writers use unforgettable for trips, holidays, events and adverts, such as «an unforgettable experience», to make the moment sound important.
exercise: «We had an unforgettable day at the seaside.» What does unforgettable mean? | *So special you will remember it for a long time | Boring and too long | Very cold and wet | Quick and easy to forget
exercise: Which word means about the same as unforgettable? | *Iconic | Tiny | Muddy | Sleepy
exercise: What does the un- in unforgettable mean? | Before | *Not | Very | Again
exercise: «The concert was an unforgettable experience.» What does the word tell you about the concert? | *It will stay in your memory for a long time | It was short and quiet | It was held indoors | It cost very little
exercise: Why might a writer use unforgettable in a story? | *To show that the moment matters a lot | To make the reader fall asleep | To show that the story has no ending | To show the story is in another language
test: «The trip was an unforgettable adventure.» What does unforgettable mean here? | Dull and very short | Lost on the way | Expensive to buy | *Special enough that you will remember it for a long time
test: Which word is made from forget and -able, with un- at the front, to mean that something cannot be easily forgotten? | Forgettery | Forgetful | Forgotten | *Unforgettable
exam: Which is the best meaning of unforgettable? | *Something so special that it stays in your memory for a long time | Something that happened yesterday | Something you can easily forget | Something that is always the same
